{"arena": "Z", "t": 1792901147.2, "seq": 76, "op": "mutate", "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "cost": 0.0005714400000000001, "parents": ["Z32"], "log": {"edges": [["progress", "goal_field", "call"]], "n_edges": 1, "editable": ["s3", "s4"], "llm": {"in": 516, "out": 931, "cache_read": 5434, "cache_write": 0, "seconds": 4.6, "stop": "end_turn"}, "reply": "This mutation caches the goal distance field once per turn in an `update()` keep, instead of recomputing `field(goals())` on every pass of the loop. The fuel saving should be large because `goals()` and `field()` are engine calls. The trade-off is that the field can be a few actions stale within a turn, for example after a champion moves or a camp is cleared.\n\n```python\nGOAL_CACHE: Field = None\n\n@gene(\"s3b\", \"goal distance field, cached once per turn in update()\", parents=[\"s3\"])\ndef goal_field() -> Field:\n    return GOAL_CACHE\n\n@gene(\"u3\", \"compute the goal distance field once at the start of each turn\", parents=[\"s3\"])\ndef update() -> None:\n    GOAL_CACHE = field(goals())\n```"}, "error": "GenomeError: line 59: gene goal_field redefined or shadows a builtin", "birth": 36, "accepted": false, "fingerprint": null}
